  "status_text": "The list is complete by two programs that agree: every cheapest circuit of the six most expensive kinds of graph at four a side is now listed (computed, not checked). One graph stands apart, the crown: all 681 of its cheapest circuits read each input exactly once and do all their sharing on gates, while the other five share any way they like. A seat tried to turn that into a proof and the list stopped it, since 24 of the 681 leave a pair unmerged and are just as small. Also checked in Lean: to represent the crown takes at least 3n AND/OR gates of fan-in at most two, from five a side on.",
